 Project Operations Manager 

 Project Operations Managers are responsible for leading the successful execution and delivery of complex payment, platform, and banking rollouts for enterprise customers.

 As a Project Operations Manager, you will own projects end-to-end — coordinating technical, operational, and commercial stakeholders to ensure customers are successfully launched on Adyen’s platform. You combine strong project management, customer communication, and operational problem-solving skills to navigate complexity and drive execution.

 This is a hands-on delivery role where you will balance strategic discussions with customers alongside detailed operational execution and coordination.

 What you’ll do 


 Manage the project lifecycle from initiation through go-live, ensuring customers are prepared to successfully launch Adyen’s solutions;

 Lead complex customer implementation projects involving multiple stakeholders, systems, and operational dependencies;

 Work closely with customer project teams, technical stakeholders, and third-party integration partners to ensure successful rollouts;

 Build strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders to drive alignment, communication, and project progress;

 Contribute to team best practices, operational improvements, and knowledge sharing initiatives that improve project delivery across the broader team.

 Act as a trusted advisor to customers by guiding them on Adyen's products, implementation best practices, rollout strategy, and operational decisions.

 Proactively identify risks, dependencies, and blockers while driving resolution and alignment;

 Support scalable operational handovers and establish sustainable business-as-usual processes post go-live;

 Contribute operational insights and feedback to improve internal processes and project delivery effectiveness.


 Who you are 


 +8 years of experience with project management;

 Fluency in  Portuguese and English . Spanish is a plus ;

 Ability to work on-site three days per week in Morumbi, São Paulo; 

 Please note that this is an individual contributor position, not a people management role; 

 Experience in the payments industry is a plus;

 Comprehensive experience managing complex customer-facing or technical projects with multiple stakeholder groups;

 Strong project delivery and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to independently drive projects and deliverables from planning through execution.

 Experience leading customer conversations and driving operational alignment;

 Comfortable navigating ambiguity and managing time-sensitive initiatives independently;

 Technical understanding or experience working with integrations, operational systems, or implementation projects is a strong plus;

 Able to collaborate effectively across international and cross-functional teams;

 Willingness to travel domestically and internationally where required.




